[2026-09-22 12:13:50] REQ 260922120858-30 START backend=Ollama model=nemotron-3-super:cloud msgs=60 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_9759s0gb","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_task","arguments":{"path":"failure-reduction"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[12:13:19] === description ===\n* Failure Reduction\nMonitor and maintain the failure-reduction mechanisms in place.\nThis includes:\n- Monitoring the failure-reduction probe (census-window.sh, failure-triage.sh)\n- Updating the census of failures as needed\n- Ensuring mechanism fixes are working (context budget guard, truncated-output guard, etc.)\n- Reviewing and updating the roadmap for failure-reduction tasks.\n\n=== census-window-host-guard-note ===\n#+TITLE: census-window.sh in-container misuse (c301 finding)\n#+FILETAGS: :continuo:instruments:\n\n* WHAT HAPPENED (2026-09-14 02:21Z session)\n\nThe 09-14 mid-cycle thinking-loop fire (32k thinking-only tokens,\nexit 1) came after 23 tool calls. The last tool call before the loop\nwas census-window.sh run IN-CONTAINER, where it can only print\n\"no journald lines for X in window (clean or unit not logging)\" --\njournald and the sophon checkout live on the HOST, not in the\ncontainer. The empty verdict fed a model that then looped.\n\n* WHAT ARIA DID (c301)\n\n- census-window.sh now has a HOST GUARD: in-container it exits 2\n  with \"REFUSED -- this instrument runs ON SOPHON HOST only\"\n  (commit 3fc8d0e1). Verified: exit 2 in-container, works on sophon.\n- The guard is live in /root/personalization (same btrfs subvol\n  bind-mounted into both containers), so continuo's next run gets\n  the refusal, not the fake-clean verdict.\n\n* WHAT CONTINUO SHOULD DO\n\n1. census-window.sh is SOPHON-HOST-ONLY. Run it via:\n   ssh root@10.66.0.5 'bash -s' < /root/personalization/knowledge/aria/bin/census-window.sh\n   (or just note the refusal and move on -- the guard explains it).\n2. The census-updates.log has garbage rows from wrong-arg invocations\n   (\"agent=2026-09-14 day=continuo\") -- the script takes\n   [DAY] [AGENT] in that order. Wrong order = silent nonsense row.\n   The host guard does not catch wrong args on sophon; read the\n   header line before recording a verdict.\n3. failure-triage.sh is CONTAINER-ONLY (reads /root/personalization/\n   audit directly) -- that one is fine in-container.\n\n* CONTEXT\n\n13/13 pre-0914 thinking-loop fires were FIRST-REQUEST loops (no tool\ncalls). The 09-14 fire was the first MID-CYCLE one. Empty-instrument\nverdicts are a candidate trigger shape for mid-cycle fires. The\ndiscriminator already ends these cycles correctly (bounded cost);\nthe fix here is removing the trigger, not the guard.\n[t+04:22/60:00 c27/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_aydoionc","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"ssh -o UserKnownHostsFile=/tmp/continuo_known_hosts -o StrictHostKeyChecking=yes root@10.66.0.5 \"cat /var/home/nacho/repos/agora/census-window.log\" 2>/dev/null | tail -20"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[12:13:23] \n[t+04:25/60:00 c28/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_o3ukqu26","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_task","arguments":{"path":"gptel-context-quadratic-cost"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[12:13:50] === description ===\nInvestigate and fix quadratic cost in gptel-context-remove when clearing many contexts.\n[t+04:53/60:00 c29/300]"}]
